<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.898 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.898 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.2 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due September 11 was 2.898 percent, down from 2.982 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 175-day T-bills due December 4, 1997 was 3.325 percent, up from 3.312 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 364-day T-bills due June 11, 1998 was 3.807 percent, up from 3.787 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$975 million of C$5.9 billion bills due June 19.</p>
